        <h2>Summary / Description</h2>
        <div class="description">
          <div>The Spaceflight-Associated Neuro-Ocular Syndrome Countermeasures (SANS CM) study consisted of six investigations sponsored by NASA's Human Research Program in partnership with the German Aerospace Center (DLR). SANS CM was carried out at the Institute of Aerospace Medicine’s :envihab facility in Cologne, Germany. </div><div><br></div><div>The study was implemented over four campaigns consisting of 12 research participants each for a total of 48 participants. The study had four protocol arms that were executed across two campaigns each. </div><div><br></div><div>Campaigns 1 and 2 </div><div><ul><li>Arm 1: Strict 6° Head-Down Tilt (HDT) + 6 hours seated countermeasure </li><li>Arm 2: Strict 6°  HDT + 6 hours Lower Body Negative Pressure (LBNP) Countermeasure</li></ul></div><div>Campaigns 3 and 4 </div><div><ul><li>Arm 3: Strict 6° HDT + exercise countermeasure</li><li>Arm 4: Strict 6° HDT (control)</li></ul><div><br></div><div>These four campaigns were conducted at the :envihab facility between September 2021 and July 2023. Each campaign consisted of the following schedule:</div></div><div><ul><li>Phase 1: 15 days of baseline data collection</li><li>Phase 2: 30 days of strict 6° head-down tilt bedrest</li><li>Phase 3: 13 days of post-bedrest recovery </li></ul></div><div><br></div><div> </div>
        </div>

